  <content>
  <note class="self-check"><para>The table below shows the revenue for the number of pizzas sold at a restaurant.</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>Number of Pizzas</emphasis></entry><entry>20</entry>
      <entry>30</entry>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry>50</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Revenue</emphasis></entry><entry>110</entry>
      <entry>160</entry>
      <entry>210</entry>
      <entry>260</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<para>Which linear model could be used to predict the revenue if 4000 pizzas were sold?</para></note>
</content>
</document>